WEBVTT

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:06.180
So we're off duty?

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:06.700
Yes.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.030
Off duty?

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:09.660
I think I've heard of that before...

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.080
What?

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.170
Oh, I know what it is, Mana-chan.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:13.410
Oh!

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.140
<i>Space Inspector</i>!

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.250
What's that?

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:20.220
We've been getting into 
retro TV programs lately.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.630
<i>Space Inspector: Off Duty</i>!

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:25.130
A tokusatsu series that defined an era.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:27.150
Sure, <i>Space Inspector</i> has that in its name,

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.870
but I'm trying to say 
we're taking a vacation.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:34.550
You've been on alert this whole time.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.640
We're going to take time off in shifts.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.940
A vacation?!

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:17.360
<b>Hair-raising! Unidentified Creature 
Spotted in the Snowy Mountains</b>

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:15.650
So why are we going to a hot spring?

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:18.110
Well, I have some connections.

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:20.360
A hot spring inn, huh?

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.640
I've never stayed at one, so I'm excited.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.220
There's a large ski resort 
close by, too, I heard.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.460
Really?!

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.970
Then I wanna try snowboarding!

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.540
I want to try that out, too.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:32.670
Let's do it together.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.460
Yeah!

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.060
We won't join you, though.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:38.000
H-Huh?

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:42.120
We have a different goal.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.440
Goal?

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:45.450
This.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:50.160
<b>The Yamajiri Hiroshi Exploration Party Series</b>

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:50.160
<b>Yeti Sighted in an Undeveloped Area 
of the Daisetsuzan Mountains!</b>

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.530
<i>The Yamajiri Hiroshi Exploration Party:</i>

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:50.160
<i>Yeti Sighted in an Undeveloped Area 
of the Daisetsuzan Mountains!</i>

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:51.980
What's that?

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.730
An old exploration variety show.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:59.650
Our exploration party is going to 
find a yeti-chin in the mountains!

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.280
So that's what's going on.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.710
So much space!

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.800
Wow! How'd you get us a room like this?

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.190
Well, I have some connections.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.380
That's Yuumi-san for you.

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:29.440
It's Altair Torte's first trip together.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:31.640
I want to make it a good experience.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:32.940
Makes sense.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.040
Thanks, Yuumi.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.480
All right, let's go find that yeti-chin!

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:38.790
Yeah!

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.100
Do you need all that equipment?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.580
Well, we're going exploring.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.450
We need to have at least this much.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.980
Mana-san is exactly right.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:53.920
Yep.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:07.100
Mana and the others are really into this.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.010
Maybe they'll really find one.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:11.440
No way.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:15.360
But that kinda looks fun, too.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:23.530
The Namori Mana exploration party, 
in search of the mysterious yeti,

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.880
has come deep into the 
snow-covered mountains.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.030
Yeti-chin!

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.820
The captain calls out to the yeti,

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:34.930
as if she's searching for 
survivors in the snow.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:38.020
I won't get mad at you, so come out!

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:40.900
I mean, as if she's trying 
to search for a runaway.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:44.860
<b>Snowboard Techniques
for Beginners</b>

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.240
Hey, Tsubame...

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:49.110
Isn't it too big a challenge 
for a newbie to start here?

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:51.060
It's fine, it's fine.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.600
I made sure to study this.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:53.930
Let's see...

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:56.840
First, you point the edge up toward the slope...

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.330
Hey, Tsubame! Like this?

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:04.870
Yeah, I think that's right...

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:12.150
We've come deep into the snow-covered 
mountains in search of a yeti,

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:14.710
but haven't been able to find any clues.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:16.640
But then...

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.080
Footprints!

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.590
Captain Mana's voice loudly echos.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:26.300
Will we finally be able to discover 
the mystery of this creature?

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:32.020
The footprints, when viewed closely, 
seem to be rabbit tracks.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:33.630
But we can't let our guard down.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:37.180
It's also possible that it's a tiny yeti-chin.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:39.420
And Captain Mana now offers a new theory!

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:41.160
Let's go look!

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.370
She's running after the footprints.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:46.560
Just how far will these footprints take us?

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.360
Ow...

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:54.120
What the heck is this?!

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:57.140
They really were there!

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:59.000
Huge yeti footprints!

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.100
That was kind of dangerous.

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.150
Those were probably bear footprints.

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:04.580
No way!

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:06.560
It wasn't a bear, no matter 
how I looked at it!

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.560
What's wrong, Yuumi? 
You're really worked up.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.990
Well, I didn't think there'd really be one.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.300
That's mean!

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:15.340
You didn't?

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:16.760
Sorry, sorry.

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:19.020
Now I totally believe you.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:19.700
Jeez...

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:21.280
Me, too.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.840
I'm excited now.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.020
Come on, calm down.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.980
If there is one, it should have 
been found a long time ago, right?

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:30.130
It's completely possible.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:33.240
What?!

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.120
Everyone from Biscuit Sirius!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.200
Are you off duty, as well?

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:42.710
I guess we're replacing you and 
returning tomorrow evening.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.160
What do you mean, "it's possible"?

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:46.420
Please tell us.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:50.430
Sorry for just barging in 
on your conversation.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:56.360
Yukie is familiar with mysteries 
and supernatural phenomenon.

00:06:56.870 --> 00:07:00.550
You're talking about a UMA, right?

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:01.520
UMA?

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:06.440
Yes, "UMA" is short for 
"unidentified mysterious animal."

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:09.560
It's basically an animal yet to be identified.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:14.140
Witness reports of UMAs range 
from shady to highly convincing,

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:18.050
and they come from all around the globe.

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:21.190
In this area, there are many 
reported sightings of the yeti,

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:26.670
as well as tracks and signs that don't 
match anything left by local wildlife.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:34.080
So that's why it's quite possible the 
footprints you saw weren't from a bear.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:37.080
We were searching for the yeti, as well.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:38.320
What?!

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.810
So you believe the yeti exists too, Niho?

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.140
I believe in Yukie, that's all.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.400
Niho...

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:53.110
Also, this skiing area started producing all 
sorts of yeti goods as their specialty.

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:54.700
There'd better be one!

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:56.480
What?!

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:00.960
This inn and the surrounding skiing area...

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:05.560
Niho-sama has been left in charge of 
the management of the Hinomiya Resort.

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:07.910
What? So the connections 
Yuumi said she had were...

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:09.180
...Niho-chan, then?

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.650
Thank you very much.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:12.840
I don't mind.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:16.230
So now we have to find a yeti.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:19.770
If you find one, let us know. 
I will give appropriate thanks.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:20.940
Thanks?

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:24.500
Niho is betting a lot of money on this yeti.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:25.950
What?!

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:28.960
Niho, we'll overheat if we stay here any longer.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:29.990
Yes.

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:33.090
As long as you're here, you're guests.

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:35.290
I will make sure you receive 
appropriate hospitality.

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:37.130
Enjoy yourselves.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.520
She was so cool.

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:46.350
That was pretty impressive.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:47.960
Hospitality?

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:53.400
This is the boat sushi meal 
provided by the owner.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:09:00.200
This is the wagyu steak 
provided by the owner.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:08.370
This is the owner's recommended 
yakisoba bread.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:11.340
That was good.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:13.770
Io-chin, the boat sushi was amazing, wasn't it?

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:14.430
Yeah.

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:18.680
That was some great 
hospitality in my tummy.

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:23.800
Oh, the futons are already laid out.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:27.420
I get to sleep next to Io-chin!

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:29.540
I don't really mind where I am.

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:32.670
Nice and warm.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.400
This feels nice.

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:38.350
Feels like fresh-baked curry bread.

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:40.690
I think I get what you mean.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:41.840
You do?

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:46.540
All right, we'll go look for the yeti-chin with 
Tsubame-chin and Io-chin tomorrow, too!

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:48.200
What? Us, too?

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:49.930
Yeah, let's go.

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:51.970
It'll be more fun with the five of us.

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:53.530
Oh, all right.

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:54.430
Io?

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:57.740
Yay! Io-chin's joining us!

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:00.010
Hey, what about you, Tsubame-chin?

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:00.900
Sure.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.520
I'll join in, too.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:04.060
I'm kind of curious.

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:05.090
All right!

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:09.420
Okay, so tomorrow, we'll be the 
Altair Torte exploration party!

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.660
We'll find that yeti-chin!

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:12.990
Yeah!

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:24.600
We've gotten two new members

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:30.980
and have forged into the mountains 
in search of the mysterious yeti.

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:35.820
It's true that the Yamajiri Hiroshi 
Exploration Party felt a lot like this.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:39.940
I didn't think she'd also be doing 
the narration and camera work.

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:42.700
Something moved over there!

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:46.360
And then Captain Mana found something!

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:48.890
There really is something there!

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:50.440
There are three of them!

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:52.790
Yeti-chin!

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:54.520
What's that?

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:56.270
Aren't those bears?

00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:57.160
It's dangerous.

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:58.410
Yeah.

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:00.030
Wait, guys!

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:06.700
Will our team run into the 
legendary yeti, after all?

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:11.410
Huh?

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:12.400
They're not here.

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:15.210
Mana-chan, did you find them?

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:16.220
No.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:18.960
That's dangerous.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:20.680
What if they had been bears?

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:21.740
It's okay.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.370
They were yeti-chin.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.740
Yeti are dangerous, too.

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:28.120
You should be more careful.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:31.260
But it doesn't look like anything's here.

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:33.900
Maybe we imagined it.

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:35.790
It's good that we did.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.080
It's really dangerous.

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:46.940
I'm... hungry...

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:47.560
Huh?

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:53.880
Akara-chin?

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:05.790
I feel alive again.

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:08.960
Thanks. This was a big help.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:13.620
You shouldn't go into snow-covered mountains
with such light clothing and no food.

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:16.240
We were planning on returning right away.

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:18.090
Why were you here?

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:22.530
I heard we could get a huge 
reward if we found the yeti.

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:24.850
I was against it, though.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:27.310
I want to see the yeti.

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:29.720
It's not that big a mountain,

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.980
so we thought we could find 
it if we just walked around.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.500
We didn't find it at all, though.

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:36.740
And so you got stuck out here, huh?

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:39.100
We knew the way back,

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:42.860
but we found some large footprints 
that couldn't be a bear's...

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:46.840
Those were the same ones we found!

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:48.510
Yeah, probably.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:52.490
So when we followed those 
footprints into a cave,

00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:53.940
there was this bear.

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:57.840
We ran as fast as we could, 
and then we got lost.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:59.510
I see.

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:01.420
The bear wasn't to blame.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.630
We're the ones that scared it.

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:07.720
So those footprints really were a bear's?

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:10.640
No, those weren't bear footprints.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:11.320
They were...

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:12.580
Hey!

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:15.150
Oh, everyone from Sirius.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:18.790
You know them, right?

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:21.880
Akara-chin, Hina-chin, and Koori-chin.

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:24.080
They almost got stuck out here.

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:25.890
I see.

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:28.680
By the way, have you found 
any clues on the yeti?

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:33.520
Akara-chin and the others found 
that those footprints led to a cave.

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:35.210
Really?

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:36.810
Yes.

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:40.830
But they said they ran 
into a bear in that cave,

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:42.640
so they might have been bear tracks.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:44.510
Where is this cave?

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:48.570
Past the ridge, way over there.

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:50.620
Let's go.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:55.530
You believe us?

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:01.320
Even if it was a bear, 
it's near our skiing resort.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:02.860
We need to take it out.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:04.770
Can we go, too?

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:05.700
Do as you wish.

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:07.090
We'll go, too.

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:07.780
No!

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:10.940
If you follow us in that light gear

00:14:10.940 --> 00:14:13.150
and we hit a blizzard, we can't save you.

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:14.260
Save...

00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:16.620
You almost got stuck up here, right?

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:22.420
Go back down the mountain.

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:32.100
Hey, Niho-chin, you should have brought 
Akara-chin and the others with us.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.240
The snowy mountains aren't that forgiving.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:35.110
Also...

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:38.410
I still don't trust them.

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:39.400
What?

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:42.600
Even if Morgana was controlling them,

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:44.740
they were enemies until just the other day.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.810
They aren't enemies anymore.

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:49.420
That might be true,

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:54.880
but I don't want to do anything dangerous 
with people I don't fully trust.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:58.290
We need time to figure them out.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.620
A single ant tunnel can collapse a dike.

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:06.340
And ants can carry five times their own weight.

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:09.060
I don't think that's related...

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:14.530
This is the cave?

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:17.180
Who knew this was nearby?

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:18.480
It's rather large.

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:22.080
The entrance sure makes you 
feel like something's here!

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:23.360
How exciting.

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:24.620
Let's go.

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:33.020
We've finally set foot into the cave 
where the yeti was spotted.

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:38.000
Will that mysterious creature 
show itself to us?

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:40.140
What are you doing?

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:41.680
We're...

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:43.250
Um, well...

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:46.230
You're the Yamajiri Hiroshi 
Exploration Party, right?

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:47.240
Huh?

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:48.320
You know it?

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:50.090
I like it, too.

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:51.860
Niho, you do too, right?

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:56.440
O-Only because you forced me to watch it.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:59.940
Didn't you buy the complete box set?

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:01.170
Really?!

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:02.820
That's surprising.

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:06.280
Well, it was somewhat interesting.

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:09.120
That's the limited edition, right?

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:10.900
Wow!

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.220
I'll let you borrow it sometime.

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:13.480
Yay!

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:15.130
Niho-sama.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:18.920
Something's there!

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:22.910
Yeti-chin?!

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:24.000
Let's go after it!

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:27.990
The yeti-chin is going to get away!

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:29.300
That's not a yeti!

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:30.230
Then it's a bear?

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:32.020
No, that's an O'bli!

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:33.010
What?

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:34.260
An O'bli?

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:36.180
Wait a second.

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:38.220
That's a huge problem!

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:43.210
Yes, I've never heard of an O'bli 
appearing in the real world.

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:44.560
What? Really?!

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:47.570
If an O'bli goes wild in the real world...

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:50.190
But if we're up against an O'bli...

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:52.490
We won't be able to handle 
it without our equipment!

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:55.430
But before it gets outside...

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:56.580
We need to do something.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:16:59.930
What's this place?

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:00.910
Crystals?

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:06.040
It disappeared?

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:08.400
I see. So that's what's going on.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:09.340
What is it?

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:13.270
Most likely, these crystals are Stella Prisms,

00:17:13.270 --> 00:17:15.380
or some sort of substance 
that works the same.

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:21.260
The O'bli are using these to come to
this world from the fifth dimension.

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:22.020
What?!

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:23.100
Let's go after it!

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:25.660
If we go to the fifth dimension,

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:28.060
we can get Tierra-sensei to send equipment.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.100
I get it!

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:30.520
Nice idea!

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:33.850
All right! Let's go, 
Altair Torte Exploration Party!

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:35.380
Biscuit Sirius, we're going, too!

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:44.250
<i>It's true that something similar to Stella Prisms 
can come to be in the real world.</i>

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:49.630
<i>It's possible that the O'bli came 
to the real world using those.</i>

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:50.980
We'll stop them here.

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:52.380
Send our equipment, quick.

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:54.680
<i>Actually...</i>

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:56.720
There's some server trouble,

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:59.940
and Biscuit Sirius's equipment 
maintenance has fallen behind.

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:01.330
This is bad, moshu!

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:02.900
Everything's on fire, moshu!

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:06.570
What? Then what about 
Altair Torte's equipment?

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:08.180
<i>That should be fine.</i>

00:18:08.510 --> 00:18:12.120
<i>Then send Altair Torte their equipment.</i>

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:13.000
What?

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:15.490
Altair Torte's there, too?

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:16.070
<i>Yes.</i>

00:18:16.460 --> 00:18:17.480
<i>Got it.</i>

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:18.510
Thank you.

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:21.290
Listen up.

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:26.340
We can't use our equipment because 
its maintenance is running late.

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:29.500
We'd like Altair Torte to take out the O'bli.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:30.570
Right.

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:32.130
We just have to do this.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:35.690
The climax to the 
Altair Torte Exploration Party!

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:38.420
We've got about one hour and 45 minutes.

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:40.120
Everyone, let's go.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:41.160
Right!

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:52.910
I wonder if they'll be okay.

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:53.530
Yeah.

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:56.200
We'll just have to leave it to them.

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:57.470
Besides,

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.660
they're more polished than before.

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:04.990
They're still a bit inefficient, but...

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:10.410
I'm not sure if they're making great 
strides, but they are growing.

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:17.680
There wasn't just one of them!

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:20.260
It's fast!

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:36.530
Are you okay?

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:38.990
Why are you here?

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:42.410
We couldn't just leave 
the mountain like that,

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.010
so we came after you.

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:47.420
Looks like this is what the yeti really were.

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:54.090
Um...

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:57.840
Thank you for saving Niho-sama.

00:19:57.840 --> 00:19:59.300
We thank you.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.740
It's not that big a deal.

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:02.360
Don't worry about it.

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:03.550
See you later.

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:21.760
Are you guys okay after that battle?

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.160
Yeah, we're fine.

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:24.020
Huh?

00:20:24.020 --> 00:20:25.740
Were Akara-chin and the others here?

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:26.590
They were.

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:27.800
I knew it.

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:31.840
But who would have thought that 
the yeti were really O'bli?

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:35.450
Yeah, they caused so much trouble...

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:36.390
Oh, yeah!

00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:39.880
Now we can't use them as the 
ski resort's specialty goods!

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:42.760
We can't talk about O'bli publicly.

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:45.260
Then the yeti goods...

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.870
We'll have to get rid of them.

00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:48.640
Can't be helped.

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:51.470
Let's think of a different idea.

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:55.660
They're pretty interesting.

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:58.910
We're all going to school together now, 
so we should be friends.

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:00.540
Sure, why not?

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:01.540
Really?

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:02.700
Yeah.

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:04.790
We're not fighting anymore.

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:08.570
What is it?

00:22:53.550 --> 00:22:55.120
I know they were getting rid of them,

00:22:55.120 --> 00:22:58.280
but they didn't have to give us so many.

00:22:58.280 --> 00:23:00.620
Mana said she wanted all of them.

00:23:00.620 --> 00:23:02.780
Hey, where is Mana-chan, anyway?

00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:04.140
This is amazing!

00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:06.740
Look! Look! Look!

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:07.880
Right here.

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:11.270
Look close, right here.

00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:13.450
What?

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:15.050
Is this for real?

00:23:15.050 --> 00:23:17.000
We need to let Niho-chin know.

00:23:17.510 --> 00:23:20.630
So we're giving all this stuff back, then?

00:23:23.570 --> 00:23:27.880
I'm sorry I said I was done 
with you last time.

00:23:28.520 --> 00:23:32.380
You do still have a use.

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:41.020
<b>Change! The Three Sisters Have Disappeared</b>

00:23:38.180 --> 00:23:41.020
"Change! The Three Sisters Have Disappeared."
